WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.700
Film Courage: You had something happen to
you which is a screenwriter’s worst nightmare

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.149
where a script of your’s was stolen?

00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:11.200
Rachel K. Ofori, Producer/Writer:&nbsp;Yes, I
had a script stolen. I have two scenarios

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:17.030
that you can say the world stolen. But the
one that I think affected me deeply was I

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:23.460
trusted people that wanted me to write and
I was 19. This was my first hire for film,

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:29.329
a film script that I am being hired to write.
I worked with people that I really trusted

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.850
and they didn’t do the wrong thing but they
didn’t protect me to make sure the wrong

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:38.510
thing didn’t happen or even ask me questions
to make sure I was thinking of it.The film

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:43.550
originally they told me Well this is not really
where we want to go. We will circle back maybe

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.809
a year from now because we are going to go
with another idea. I said Okay, no problem.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:51.129
I enjoyed the experience. I got to write a
film script start-to-finish and just kind

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:56.989
of waited.&nbsp;Then I saw the film. It was maybe
two or three years later and it was a little

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:02.190
different but it was like “Okay? I wrote
that line!” You know, one of those moments.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:07.450
So I think it was a horrible experience but
I can’t say I’m glad it happened but a

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:11.500
lot of goodness came out of it. It caused
me to be so much more prudent and so much

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:16.700
more watchful and wise which is great for
personal use but also being someone on the

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.399
other end now, hiring writers and so forth
and even something I am working on right now

00:01:21.399 --> 00:01:25.680
in pre-production, I want to educate every
young writer because it’s something that

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.740
no one is going to…I can’t say no one…but
there aren’t many people that are not going

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:34.640
to want to use you for your gift and that’s
a good thing.&nbsp;But you’ve got to be sure

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.840
that they use you in a way that you are comfortable
with being used. So its’ like it’s fine,

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.649
your gifts are here to be used and shown so
don’t feel like Oh, they are using me! That’s

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:46.420
fine, just put limits and boundaries in that
and that comes in with legal. So most of these

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:51.280
young writers…most of them unless they got
into a place where they shot up to the top

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.899
or they can have an agent or a lawyer and
this and that (somebody watching out for them)

00:01:54.899 --> 00:01:58.520
they have no clue what paperwork needs to
be put in place and how that paperwork needs

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:02.579
to be worded to where they’re protected
and because of what I went through I researched

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:06.520
that and I didn’t just research it like
“Now I know,” but I also always bounced

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.869
it off of a lawyer. Even when I am giving
advice. I’m like “Hey this guy is in this

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:14.290
and does this clause mean this?” Because
that is what I am thinking, so just being

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:21.240
very watchful of it and also I am super protective
of writers. Like Argg! It’s like a Mama

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:26.510
Bear thing that comes out and a project that
I’m working on right now the writer called

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:31.659
me just a couple of days ago and “I just
want to thank you. You have been there every

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:36.730
step of the way. You weren’t even on the
project yet.” This is like way before pre-production,

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:44.080
just conversations. And he was like I just
felt so safe and I couldn’t have had a better

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:49.140
compliment than that. That a writer who was
around me felt safe because I experienced

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.840
the other way around.&nbsp;I want to make sure
that anyone around my presence, writers, producers

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.370
(whatever it is) they feel safe and they feel
that they can trust (like I did) but also

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:02.190
get the outcome that their trust actually
mattered and it was the right person to trust.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:06.500
I never want to hurt that in someone. That
is something that I’m very mindful of and

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:11.860
I don’t think there’s an opportunity for
us to make bad decisions that every person

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:17.981
has that like maybe greed or whatever the
thing is that you see great people fall. When

00:03:17.981 --> 00:03:23.459
you’ve already experienced what great people
do (what they can do in power) but you’ve

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:26.260
been on the other end of that, when you get
some power, you are going to be more mindful

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:31.189
of how you treat people.So I can say that
experience of having a script stolen, makes

00:03:31.189 --> 00:03:35.230
me a better leader, makes me a better producer,
makes me a better writer, makes me a better

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:40.411
person because I know these people weren’t
bad people but they saw an opportunity and

00:03:40.411 --> 00:03:42.939
they are like “Well we don’t have to really
pay her anymore. We don’t have to bring

00:03:42.939 --> 00:03:46.680
her in. She is not owed any points. Let’s
just go, don’t even tell her.” That can

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:52.110
happen when you have greed. So I don’t look
or think of them as horrible people, I think

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:58.750
of them as people who succumbed to greed or
because they could. We all want a sense of

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:03.519
power and they used it in the wrong way. So
it helps me use it in the right way more often

00:04:03.519 --> 00:04:10.220
and with more intention.&nbsp;Film Courage: What
are some tips…aside from having legal look

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:17.441
over a contract or even emails…what are
some signs (like a red flag) that a writer

00:04:17.441 --> 00:04:27.110
should be aware of?Rachel: Red flags for young
writers or anyone is people asking you for

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:33.650
things that 1) You don’t understand or 2).
You didn’t agree with already. So it’s

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:37.290
like usually how it happens is they kind of
sneak it in there. It’s like Okay we have

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:41.350
an agreement and then it’s like “Hey can
you also do such-and-such.” And young writers

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.680
especially they are like “I can’t wait
to do these things.” So they just do it.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.730
Don’t do it. Be okay or you can start writing
it, start working with it, but don’t tell

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:53.390
them. Don’t say okay. Don’t say absolutely.
Just say “Oh sure. Just have whoever call

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:57.470
me so we can change the contract.” You can
do it in such a way that you don’t seem

00:04:57.470 --> 00:05:02.110
like you’re checking them. Just make it
seem like you’re just being helpful “I’ll

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:05.190
take care of it. I can talk to whoever, just
let me know. Do I need to sign something else?”

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:09.690
Ask an innocent question like that and I’ll
tell you those people will adjust their movements.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:13.810
Just say “Oh great sure. Do I need to sign
something different?” If they say “No.”

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:18.000
That will be the next red flag that it’s
not only that they were maybe negligent, they

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.390
were probably trying to take advantage of
you. Because you do have to sign something.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:25.000
There needs to be an adjustment and if they’re
not willing to do that you don’t need to

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.840
be in the situation.&nbsp;Or stay in the situation
because you know we have to be in places sometimes

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:33.870
where Okay, be amongst the snakes but like
the Bible says be a dove. We don’t need

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:37.600
to act like a snake so we need to know how
the snakes move. Be there and just keep very

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.650
watch and care on what you are doing and presenting
to them.&nbsp;So you are like “Hey, where is

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.740
that such and such?” “Oh yeah, I have
it pretty much ready, I just need whatever

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:49.230
paper I need to sign.” Bring it up later.
You don’t have to fight them or argue with

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:54.510
them.&nbsp;I see another thing young writers do
where “I read that such-and-such” or “my

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:57.560
friend said such-and-such.” And it’s like
now you’re just going to come off as a jerk

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:01.270
and that person might have been innocent in
this situation. So just come from an inquisitive

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:08.160
place and then record that response. I’m
not saying record that scenario or have a

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.620
phone recorder of whatever but after they
responded, write it down so you can then think

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:16.440
about it later and then talk about it with
a friend. Of course it’s great to talk it

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.650
over with someone in the industry but just
hearing yourself out loud talk to someone

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:24.950
helps. You kind of understand where someone
is moving, so write it down exactly how they

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:28.750
said. Send a text to yourself. I do Notes
all day with phone calls even when I am sitting

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:32.830
on a call, I am writing down certain moments
in the call just to kind of be “What just

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:39.950
happened here?”&nbsp;Just be mindful of requests
and seeing (not responding) but seeing how

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:44.600
they respond to you pushing back on their
requests in any capacity and that will be

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:48.630
a telltale sign that this is probably going
to be a situation where people are not going

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:52.210
to protect you. So you can stay in it but
be ready to protect yourself or bring someone

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:56.110
else in to protect you.Film Courage: I like
that! Let’s take the scenario where the

00:06:56.110 --> 00:07:01.940
person tries to turn it around on you and
make it seem like you’re the one that’s

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:06.270
the problem. So let’s say they say “Well
I only operate with a handshake and I go on

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:09.960
good faith like that. And I would hope you
would trust me?” And that makes you feel

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:15.190
like “Oh, wow. Now this makes me look mistrustful.”
So you would almost want to prove to them

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:18.790
“Okay, yes that’s fine, we’ll do that.”
How do you deal with when they try to turn

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.650
it around (as has happened to a lot of people)
and make it seem like it doesn’t need to

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:31.410
be changed or initialed or noted?Rachel: I
think first understand that your trust has

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:36.820
to be rooted in truth. So trust is built.
You don’t owe anyone it, just have that

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:41.010
stance. I don’t owe trust to anyone. They
have to build it and I have to build it for

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:44.391
them. They don’t have to trust me to write
and go do my job. Don’t act like “I’m

00:07:44.391 --> 00:07:48.350
a writer. I’ve done such-and-such.” Either
way you have to come with humility. But trust

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:51.850
has to be earned. Now you don’t have to
tell them that but you have to have that stance.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:56.510
So let’s say someone says something like
that where it’s “Well I operate on a handshake

00:07:56.510 --> 00:08:00.380
and I hope you trust me.” “Absolutely,
I hope so too. So I’m going to start writing

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:03.910
on this and just whenever you’re ready you
can give me a piece of paper and you’re

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.320
going to put this in writing and then I can
deliver it.” It’s just for me and there

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.940
are so many people out here that you can’t
trust, right?” Like kind of connect with

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:15.051
them… “Right?” And then they are like&nbsp;…what
crazy person wouldn’t be like “No, trust

00:08:15.051 --> 00:08:18.980
everyone.” Give them truth and if your trust
is rooted in truth and you stay in a place

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:23.340
of truth, you won’t come off as combative
or difficult. Just stay in a place of truth.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:27.610
“There are so many people out here, right?”
“Yeah, I get it.” “So yeah for me I’m

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:31.660
going to start moving (sure) but I just can’t
deliver anything until that piece of paper

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:35.070
only because I’ve seen so many crazy things
happen…And I don’t think that would be

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:38.820
you? I have to put those things in there to
alleviate something that could end up being

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:44.220
conflict.” But still trust has to be earned,
so let them earn it. And also have that same

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:49.690
stance on you. If you’re not making deadlines,
if you’re not giving them proofs of things

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:54.250
and giving them the types of examples that
they wanted, providing them with enough people

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:57.770
that they can call and say “Yeah, you’re
great.” Whatever the case may be, don’t

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:01.330
be offended when they are not trusting for
you either. So you have to trust. You are

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:06.630
not owed it and you don’t owe it to anyone
but still I operate in the space of for building

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:12.710
it I am going to try and confront them with
truth not in confrontation in a negative way.

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:16.390
So I would say that is the way to deal with
it. Just kind of respond very graciously but

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:20.570
also then bring them the truth and they can’t
disagree with you which is “A lot of crazy

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.200
things happen here, right?” And then go
from there.

